viation" target="gram:neuenglisch"><abbr>neuengl.</abbr></ref></hi>] <hi rend="italic">vors <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:Object"><abbr>Object</abbr></ref>, das ein Teil der <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:Person"><abbr>Person</abbr></ref>, deren Dativ im Deutschen <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:steht"><abbr>steht</abbr></ref>:</hi> ceorfan of his nosu <hi rend="italic">ihm die N.</hi> <ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 30,5 [<hi rend="italic">wie Deutsch</hi> ceorfe him þa handa 30,4] | <hi rend="italic">pleonastisch, behufs Verdeutlichung, eingefügt:</hi> gif hwa oðrum his eage oðdo <ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> <ref type="lawCode" target="law:El">El</ref> 19 | gif mon men (his <ref type="lawCode" target="law:H">H</ref>) eage ofaslea <ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 47 ‖ (his <ref type="lawCode" target="law:H">H</ref>) wæpnu syllan 42,1 | gecyðan mid (his <ref type="lawCode" target="law:H">H</ref>) aðe <ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 16 | þegn þe his socne hæbbe <ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 71,3 <hi rend="bold">5</hi>) þe + his <hi rend="italic">cuius <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:siehe"><abbr>s.</abbr></ref></hi> Relativ <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:Nummer"><abbr>n.</abbr></ref></hi> D</dictScrap>
